# ==================================================================
# Line-ending policy for files that are executed or mounted into a container.
# ==================================================================
# This repository is developed on Windows with `core.autocrlf=true`, which
# checks text files out with CRLF. That is fine for C# and TypeScript, but it
# silently breaks shell scripts:
#
#   docker/init-db-least-privilege-passwords.sh is bind-mounted into
#   postgres:16-alpine and executed by the image entrypoint. A CRLF working
#   copy turns its `#!/bin/sh` shebang into `#!/bin/sh\r`, the kernel fails
#   to resolve the interpreter, and a brand new database volume never
#   finishes initialising:
#       env: can't execute 'bash'   /  ': No such file or directory'
#
# Pinning `eol=lf` makes the working-tree copy LF regardless of the
# developer's core.autocrlf setting, so the file is executable on the
# developer's machine and inside the container. The index content is
# unchanged (already LF), so this introduces no diff to existing files.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Docker entrypoint scripts are executed directly by the postgres image, so
# they additionally need the executable bit recorded in the index.
docker/*.sh text eol=lf
scripts/*.sh text eol=lf
